{
  "slug": "universal-basic-compute",
  "name": "Universal Basic Compute",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Domain-agnostic agent toolkit for discovering and assembling free-tier resources into working outcomes. You state a goal; the master agent decomposes it into the minimum viable resource set, discovers and verifies free-tier services that can fulfill each component, and produces a concrete recipe to deploy the outcome. Ships with a compute domain (free-tier cloud services into deployed software) and self-expands into new domains — education, health, finance — as users bring new goals. Built around a six-agent protocol (master, discovery, verification, assembly, deployment, monitoring) with credential management, capability fingerprinting, and recipe versioning. Designed for people who want the outcome, not the procurement journey.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **6 agents**, **4 commands** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `bricolage` (Assemble free-tier resources into working outcomes across any domain)\n- **Agents** (6): `assembler` (The builder agent), `discovery` (Researches and creates new Bricolage domains), `guide` (Guides users through acquiring access to resources — creating accounts, getting API keys, enrolling in courses, or any…), `infra` (Helps users set up agent infrastructure on their own provisioned free compute), `master` (The master orchestrator for the Bricolage toolkit), `planner` (Analyzes a user's goal and selects the best free resources from a domain's catalog to achieve it)\n- **Commands** (4): `build`, `explore`, `setup`, `status`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `bricolage`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install universal-basic-compute@claude-community` from `chiKeka/ubc-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "agent": 6,
    "command": 4,
    "mcp": 1
  },
